    "text": "By Kearney Public Schools ,\n13 hours ago KEARNEY — Kearney High School student Tessa Buescher, a member of the Class of 2027, represented Nebraska at the 2026 SkillsUSA National Leadership & Skills Conference, earning an impressive 10th-place finish in the Basic Health Care Skills competition. As Nebraska’s state champion in the event, Buescher competed against many... Read full article",
